{
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "$schema": "https://docs.oasis-open.org/sarif/sarif/v2.1.0/errata01/os/schemas/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "grype",
          "version": "0.119.0",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-82560-perl-base",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-82560 high vulnerability for perl-base package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Pod::Text versions before 6.1.1 for Perl allow CPU and memory exhaustion formatting a POD document whose =over nesting drives the margin to the output width.  Each =over adds its indent to the margin, which wrap() subtracts from the output width to get the space available for text. When that space reaches zero, the line-splitting substitution matches the empty string, and the loop consumes no input while appending the margin padding on every pass.  Formatting an attacker-supplied POD document never returns, and the output grows until memory is exhausted."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-82560",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-82560\nSeverity: high\nPackage: perl-base\nVersion: 5.42.3-1\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-82560](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-82560)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-82560**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | perl-base  | 5.42.3-1  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-82560](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-82560)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/perl-base@5.42.3-1?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian\u0026upstream=perl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2017-17740-libldap2",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2017-17740 low vulnerability for libldap2 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "contrib/slapd-modules/nops/nops.c in OpenLDAP through 2.4.45, when both the nops module and the memberof overlay are enabled, attempts to free a buffer that was allocated on the stack, which allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service (slapd crash) via a member MODDN operation."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2017-17740",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2017-17740\nSeverity: low\nPackage: libldap2\nVersion: 2.6.14+dfsg-2\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2017-17740](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2017-17740)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2017-17740**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| low  | libldap2  | 2.6.14+dfsg-2  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2017-17740](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2017-17740)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libldap2@2.6.14%2Bdfsg-2?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian\u0026upstream=openldap"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-85091-zlib1g",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-85091 high vulnerability for zlib1g package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "zlib versions 1.3.1.2 through 1.3.2 contain a heap buffer overflow vulnerability in the gz_vacate() function when processing non-blocking gzwrite() operations with stale external buffer pointers. Attackers can trigger the overflow by calling gzprintf() or gzvprintf() after a write stall, causing an unchecked memmove() to write beyond the internal input buffer boundary."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-85091",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-85091\nSeverity: high\nPackage: zlib1g\nVersion: 1:1.3.dfsg+really1.3.2-3\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-85091](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-85091)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-85091**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | zlib1g  | 1:1.3.dfsg+really1.3.2-3  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-85091](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-85091)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/zlib1g@1%3A1.3.dfsg%2Breally1.3.2-3?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian\u0026upstream=zlib"
                ],
                "security-severity": "8.3"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2018-20796-libc-bin",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2018-20796 low vulnerability for libc-bin package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the GNU C Library (aka glibc or libc6) through 2.29, check_dst_limits_calc_pos_1 in posix/regexec.c has Uncontrolled Recursion, as demonstrated by '(\\227|)(\\\\1\\\\1|t1|\\\\\\2537)+' in grep."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2018-20796",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2018-20796\nSeverity: low\nPackage: libc-bin\nVersion: 2.43-5\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2018-20796](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2018-20796)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2018-20796**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| low  | libc-bin  | 2.43-5  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2018-20796](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2018-20796)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libc-bin@2.43-5?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian\u0026upstream=glibc"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
